# Structural Verilog (IEEE 1364): the netlist as modules that instantiate
# each other, for a digital flow or a viewer of the hierarchy. It is
# written, never read.
#
# The top level is a module named by the first word of the title (`top`
# without one), then a module for each subcircuit, ports in pin order. A
# port's direction is what the instances inside do with it, through every
# level: an output where one drives it, an input where all only read it,
# an inout where nothing says (src/writer/modules.zig). Each module
# declares a wire for each of its other nets, sorted. An instance names its
# connections by port, `.P(net)`, never by position; the bits of a bus
# port are joined `{a, b}`. A name outside [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_$]*, or
# one that is a keyword, is escaped: a backslash before it, a blank after
# it (`wire \input ;`).
#
# The leaves are `verilog` instances; the text of their module, where the
# netlist gives it, is written once after the modules. Any other device
# has no form here: an error. Sources, analyses, outputs, options, models
# and parameters describe a simulation, not the structure: each is left
# out with a note, and so are the parameters of an instance (`#(...)` is
# never written).

dialect verilog

lexer
  case      sensitive
  title     yes "// "
  comment   line "//"
end

modules
  open     "module {name} ({ports});"
  port     "  {dir} {port};"
  net      "  wire {net};"
  instance "  {master} {name} ({pins});"
  pin      ".{port}({net})"
  join     ", "
  bus      "{" "}"
  close    "endmodule"
  dirs     "input" "output" "inout"
end

# A name: an identifier, else escaped whole. The keywords are IEEE 1800-2017's
# (Annex B), which hold IEEE 1364-2005's.
names
  ident    "A-Za-z_" "A-Za-z0-9_$"
  escape   whole "\" " "
  keywords accept_on alias always always_comb always_ff always_latch and assert assign
  keywords assume automatic before begin bind bins binsof bit break buf bufif0 bufif1 byte
  keywords case casex casez cell chandle checker class clocking cmos config const constraint
  keywords context continue cover covergroup coverpoint cross deassign default defparam
  keywords design disable dist do edge else end endcase endchecker endclass endclocking
  keywords endconfig endfunction endgenerate endgroup endinterface endmodule endpackage
  keywords endprimitive endprogram endproperty endspecify endsequence endtable endtask enum
  keywords event eventually expect export extends extern final first_match for force foreach
  keywords forever fork forkjoin function generate genvar global highz0 highz1 if iff ifnone
  keywords ignore_bins illegal_bins implements implies import incdir include initial inout
  keywords input inside instance int integer interconnect interface intersect join join_any
  keywords join_none large let liblist library local localparam logic longint macromodule
  keywords matches medium modport module nand negedge nettype new nexttime nmos nor
  keywords noshowcancelled not notif0 notif1 null or output package packed parameter pmos
  keywords posedge primitive priority program property protected pull0 pull1 pulldown pullup
  keywords pulsestyle_ondetect pulsestyle_onevent pure rand randc randcase randsequence rcmos
  keywords real realtime ref reg reject_on release repeat restrict return rnmos rpmos rtran
  keywords rtranif0 rtranif1 s_always s_eventually s_nexttime s_until s_until_with scalared
  keywords sequence shortint shortreal showcancelled signed small soft solve specify
  keywords specparam static string strong strong0 strong1 struct super supply0 supply1
  keywords sync_accept_on sync_reject_on table tagged task this throughout time timeprecision
  keywords timeunit tran tranif0 tranif1 tri tri0 tri1 triand trior trireg type typedef union
  keywords unique unique0 unsigned until until_with untyped use uwire var vectored virtual
  keywords void wait wait_order wand weak weak0 weak1 while wildcard wire with within wor
  keywords xnor xor
end

inert instance params : structural Verilog connects modules; a module's parameters (`#(...)`) are not written
inert verilog params : structural Verilog connects modules; a bridge's parameters are the simulator's

# What describes a simulation, not the structure: a note, once a kind.
inert vsource : {to} is the circuit's structure; a source is a stimulus of its simulation
inert isource : {to} is the circuit's structure; a source is a stimulus of its simulation
inert model : {to} is the circuit's structure; a leaf is a Verilog module, not a model card
inert param : {to} is the circuit's structure; parameters are not written
inert func : {to} is the circuit's structure; parameters are not written
inert global : {to} is the circuit's structure; a global net is a port of each module that uses it
inert hdl : {to} is the circuit's structure; a Verilog-A source is a simulator's
inert options : {to} is the circuit's structure; an option changes nothing in it
inert save : {to} is the circuit's structure; an output changes nothing in it
inert print : {to} is the circuit's structure; an output changes nothing in it
inert ic : {to} is the circuit's structure; an initial condition changes nothing in it
inert nodeset : {to} is the circuit's structure; an initial guess changes nothing in it
inert measure : {to} is the circuit's structure; a measurement changes nothing in it
inert fft : {to} is the circuit's structure; an output changes nothing in it
inert simctl : {to} is the circuit's structure; a simulator command changes nothing in it
inert csparam : {to} is the circuit's structure; a script's parameter changes nothing in it
inert script : {to} is the circuit's structure; a control script changes nothing in it
inert op : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert dc : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert ac : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert tran : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert noise : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert tf : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert pz : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert sens : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert disto : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert four : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert hb : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert sp : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert pss : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert stb : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert pac : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert pnoise : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert pxf : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert psp : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert xf : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert dcmatch : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert trannoise : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert phasenoise : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert envelope : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert qpss : {to} is the circuit's structure; an analysis changes nothing in it
inert step : {to} is the circuit's structure; a sweep changes nothing in it
inert data : {to} is the circuit's structure; a sweep's table changes nothing in it
inert alter : {to} is the circuit's structure; a rerun changes nothing in it
inert montecarlo : {to} is the circuit's structure; a Monte Carlo run changes nothing in it
inert optimize : {to} is the circuit's structure; an optimization changes nothing in it
inert statistics : {to} is the circuit's structure; a statistics block changes nothing in it
inert statgroup : {to} is the circuit's structure; a statistics block changes nothing in it
inert vary : {to} is the circuit's structure; a variation changes nothing in it
inert correlate : {to} is the circuit's structure; a correlation changes nothing in it
inert pattern : {to} is the circuit's structure; a pattern source's table changes nothing in it
inert embed : {to} is the circuit's structure; an embedded file changes nothing in it

# What would change the structure, and has no form here.
no resistor : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no capacitor : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no inductor : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no mutual : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no bsource : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no vcvs : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no vccs : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no cccs : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no ccvs : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no diode : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no bjt : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no mosfet : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no jfet : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no mesfet : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no vswitch : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no cswitch : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no tline : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no device : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances), not Verilog-A ones
no xspice : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no lossyline : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no ctlsrc : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no relay : structural Verilog holds only modules; its leaves are digital Verilog modules (verilog instances)
no include : structural Verilog is written as one file; translate the project with `sprack project`, or inline the include
no lib : structural Verilog is written as one file; translate the project with `sprack project`, or inline the library
no libsection : structural Verilog has no library sections
no library : structural Verilog has no library sections
no cond_if : structural Verilog has no conditional blocks
no cond_elif : structural Verilog has no conditional blocks
no cond_else : structural Verilog has no conditional blocks
no native : the statement is another dialect's own, which no kind holds; only that dialect writes it
